* ============================================================================
*  1N5819  -  Schottky diode, 40 V / 1 A, DO-41         (cabinet L1, drawer E1)
* ============================================================================
*  The free-wheeling (flyback) diode across the fan.  Written as a sub-circuit
*  so the terminal order is spelled out explicitly: KiCad's diode symbol pin 1
*  is the cathode (K) and pin 2 is the anode (A), and this keeps that mapping
*  unambiguous for ngspice.
*
*      anode (A) on the switching node (/DRAIN)
*      cathode (K) on the +12 V rail
*
*  Fit to the 1N5819 datasheet:
*
*      Vf at 0.15 A  ~ 0.35 V   ->  is = 1e-7, rs = 0.05 gives 0.38 V
*      Vf at 1 A     ~ 0.47 V   (datasheet max 0.5 V)
*      Vr max 40 V, and essentially no reverse recovery - which is exactly why a
*      Schottky is the right choice for a fan that is being chopped at 100 Hz to
*      a few kHz.
*
*  KiCad reads this file through D1's "Sim.Library" / "Sim.Name" fields.
* ============================================================================
.subckt diode_schottky K A
Dint A K diode_schottky_model
.model diode_schottky_model d(is=1e-7 rs=0.05 bv=40 ibv=100u)
.ends
